{"text": "Scientific developments and technologies in medical practice. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Have brought us enormous progress. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In the treatment and prevention of infectious diseases. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The discovery of penicillin in 1928 by Alexander Fleming. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> For which he later received the Nobel Prize. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Was one of the biggest breakthroughs. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In the battle against infectious diseases. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Edward Jenner discovered around 1796. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> That humans were protected. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Against the deadly smallpox virus. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> After exposure to the cowpox virus. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Which is harmless to humans. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Vaccines developed in laboratories. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Have contributed enormously. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> To the reduction of the burden of bacterial and viral diseases. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And have even led to the elimination of poxvirus. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> For other infectious diseases. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> For example cholera and malaria. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Control and hygiene management measures have reduced their burden. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> While for others. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Treatment therapies turned viral diseases that were deadly. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Into chronic manageable diseases.", "alignment": {"characters": ["S", "c", "i", "e", "n", "t", "i", "f", "i", "c", " ", "d", "e", "v", "e", "l", "o", "p", "m", "e", "n", "t", "s", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "t", "e", "c", "h", "n", "o", "l", "o", "g", "i", "e", "s", " ", "i", "n", " ", "m", "e", "d", "i", "c", "a", "l", " ", "p", "r", "a", "c", "t", "i", "c", "e", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "H", "a", "v", "e", " ", "b", "r", "o", "u", "g", "h", "t", " ", "u", "s", " ", "e", "n", "o", "r", "m", "o"